# wordcount reads no environment variables.
#
# The tool is a standard-library-only script: it takes one file path on the
# command line, reads it as UTF-8, prints the word count on stdout and exits.
# There is no configuration file, no secret, no service and no stored state,
# so `cp .env.example .env` changes nothing and everything still runs.
#
# The only optional environment variable is NO_COLOR (see https://no-color.org):
# setting it to any value keeps the terminal diagnostic labels plain, which is
# already the default whenever stderr is not a terminal.
